    "Sequences are everywhere: audio, text, sensor readings, the joint angles of someone doing a squat.": "clips/782191d434ec8cdc.mp3",
    "For years, the default tool for modelling them was the recurrent neural network, or RNN.": "clips/61530304406b1097.mp3",
    "It reads the sequence one step at a time, carrying a hidden state h forward from each step to the next.": "clips/22d9cbc5439f2d75.mp3",
    "Step t can't start until step t minus one has finished. Long sequences mean long chains: slow to train, and gradients that fade or explode on their way back.": "clips/680c8681ffa81092.mp3",
    "In 2018, Shaojie Bai, J. Zico Kolter and Vladlen Koltun ran a careful head-to-head comparison.": "clips/bf6d675334d7ed67.mp3",
    "Generic convolutional networks against LSTMs and GRUs, on the recurrent networks' home turf.": "clips/6bb58af3f0ace944.mp3",
